IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 29/6/2026 to 20/10/2026" (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (2) -- s 241: lodging a supplementary document or replacement document. LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- Reading a result (the rule of 2026-10-29): JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is "the TEXT says no in its own words"; NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Every "no" branch carries `-- FALSE-kind (...)`, every "not covered" branch `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.
-- Periods: "within N days from the date of lodgment" is a deadline, so an act on the day of lodgment or later up to the last day is in time (fork F9); business days come from sfa-periods.l4 (P8) with the public holidays supplied.
-- A duty is answered as "has the person done what the text requires": JUST TRUE done in time, JUST FALSE not done or late, NOTHING where the duty is not shown to arise (the six site-by-site questions of the Guide: fork F18).
-- A "where" paragraph is first answered as "is the person bound by it" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b): JUST FALSE when the "where" fails).

-- inert (reason 1), lines 39096-39096: s 241 marginal heading: not operative.
-- repealed or blank in this text, lines 39238-39238: s 241(6A): "[Deleted by Act 1 of 2005]".

§ `s 241(1) to (1C): when a supplementary or replacement document may be lodged`

-- s 241(1): the person may lodge a supplementary or replacement document. A power whose "If" gate may fail: the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit (1): NOTHING (fork F16).
-- src:39098 | 241.—(1) If, after a prospectus or profile statement is registered but
-- src:39099 | before the close of the offer of securities or securities‑based
-- src:39100 | derivatives contracts, the person making that offer becomes aware
-- src:39101 | of —
-- src:39103 | (a) a false or misleading statement in the prospectus or profile
-- src:39104 | statement;
-- src:39106 | (b) an omission from the prospectus of any information that
-- src:39107 | should have been included in it under section 243, or an
-- src:39108 | omission from the profile statement of any information that
-- src:39109 | should have been included in it under section 246, as the
-- src:39110 | case may be; or
-- src:39112 | (c) a new circumstance that —
-- src:39114 | (i) has arisen since the prospectus or profile statement
-- src:39115 | was lodged with the Authority; and
-- src:39117 | (ii) would have been required by —
-- src:39119 | (A) section 243 to be included in the prospectus; or
-- src:39121 | (B) section 246 to be included in the profile
-- src:39122 | statement,
-- src:39124 | (ii) if it had arisen before the prospectus or the profile
-- src:39125 | statement (as the case may be) was lodged,
-- src:39127 | and that is materially adverse from the point of view of an investor,
-- src:39128 | the person may lodge a supplementary or replacement prospectus, or
-- src:39129 | a supplementary or replacement profile statement (called in this
-- src:39134 | section a supplementary or replacement document, as the case may
-- src:39135 | be), with the Authority.
@ref s 241(1) (src:39098-39135)
GIVEN
    `the prospectus or profile statement has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the prospectus or profile statement been registered by the Authority?
    `the offer has not yet closed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts not yet closed?
    `the person making the offer is aware of a false or misleading statement in the prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you aware of a false or misleading statement in the prospectus or profile statement?
    `the person making the offer is aware of an omission of information that should have been included under section 243 or section 246` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you aware of an omission from the prospectus of information that should have been included under section 243, or from the profile statement of information that should have been included under section 246?
    `the person making the offer is aware of a new circumstance that has arisen since the prospectus or profile statement was lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you aware of a new circumstance that has arisen since the prospectus or profile statement was lodged with the Authority?
    `the new circumstance would have been required by section 243 or section 246 to be included had it arisen before the lodgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would section 243 (for a prospectus) or section 246 (for a profile statement) have required the new circumstance to be included, had it arisen before the prospectus or profile statement was lodged?
    `the matter is materially adverse from the point of view of an investor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter materially adverse from the point of view of an investor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F16 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 241(1) the person making the offer may lodge a supplementary or replacement document` MEANS
    IF `the prospectus or profile statement has been registered` AND `the offer has not yet closed` AND (`the person making the offer is aware of a false or misleading statement in the prospectus or profile statement` OR `the person making the offer is aware of an omission of information that should have been included under section 243 or section 246` OR (`the person making the offer is aware of a new circumstance that has arisen since the prospectus or profile statement was lodged with the Authority` AND `the new circumstance would have been required by section 243 or section 246 to be included had it arisen before the lodgment`)) AND `the matter is materially adverse from the point of view of an investor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If, after a prospectus or profile statement is registered but before the close of the offer ... the person may lodge a supplementary or replacement prospectus, or a supplementary or replacement profile statement"  -- GRANT-RULING (1): an "if" gate failed on a function named for a power; the other reading is JUST FALSE

-- s 241(1A): the base prospectus or base profile statement may be updated within 24 months, provided no offer is subsisting. The "If" gate is a grant gate (NOTHING); "provided that" closes the grant (JUST FALSE), fork F17.
-- src:39139 | (1A) If, after a base prospectus or a base profile statement referred
-- src:39140 | to in section 240A is registered but before the expiration of 24 months
-- src:39141 | from the registration of the base prospectus by the Authority, the
-- src:39142 | person making that offer intends to update any information or include
-- src:39143 | any new information in the base prospectus or base profile statement,
-- src:39144 | the person may lodge a supplementary or replacement document with
-- src:39145 | the Authority, provided that no offer to which the base prospectus or
-- src:39146 | base profile statement relates is subsisting at the time of the lodgment.
@ref s 241(1A) (src:39139-39146)
GIVEN
    `the base prospectus or base profile statement referred to in section 240A has been registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the base prospectus or base profile statement referred to in section 240A been registered by the Authority?
    `the date the base prospectus was registered` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Authority register the base prospectus?
    `the date of the lodgment` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you lodge the supplementary or replacement document?
    `the person making the offer intends to update any information or include any new information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you intend to update any information in, or include any new information in, the base prospectus or base profile statement?
    `an offer to which the base prospectus or base profile statement relates is subsisting at the time of the lodgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any offer to which the base prospectus or base profile statement relates subsisting at the time of the lodgment (section 241(1C) says when an offer is not treated as subsisting)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F17 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 241(1A) the person making the offer may lodge a supplementary or replacement document for a base prospectus or base profile statement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the base prospectus or base profile statement referred to in section 240A has been registered`) OR (NOT (`period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date the base prospectus was registered` `the date of the lodgment` 24 Months)) OR (NOT `the person making the offer intends to update any information or include any new information`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If, after a base prospectus or a base profile statement referred to in section 240A is registered but before the expiration of 24 months from the registration of the base prospectus by the Authority, the person making that offer intends to update any information or include any new information ... the person may lodge a supplementary or replacement document"  -- GRANT-RULING (1): an "if" gate failed on a function named for a power; the other reading is JUST FALSE
        IF `an offer to which the base prospectus or base profile statement relates is subsisting at the time of the lodgment`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided that no offer to which the base prospectus or base profile statement relates is subsisting at the time of the lodgment"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 241(1B): subsections (7) to (16) do not apply to a document lodged under subsection (1A). A flat negative.
-- src:39148 | (1B) Subsections (7) to (16) do not apply to a supplementary or
-- src:39149 | replacement document which is lodged under subsection (1A).
@ref s 241(1B) (src:39148-39149)
GIVEN
    `the document is lodged under subsection (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the supplementary or replacement document lodged under section 241(1A) (an update of a base prospectus or base profile statement)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(1B) subsections (7) to (16) apply to the document` MEANS
    IF `the document is lodged under subsection (1A)`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (7) to (16) do not apply to a supplementary or replacement document which is lodged under subsection (1A)"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative names the document lodged under subsection (1A) and says nothing of any other document

-- s 241(1C): when an offer is not treated as subsisting. "is not treated as subsisting if" is a one-way "if": a failed "if" is the text's no (reading (a)).
-- src:39151 | (1C) For the purposes of subsection (1A), an offer is not treated as
-- src:39152 | subsisting if —
-- src:39154 | (a) a pricing statement in respect of the offer of debentures or
-- src:39155 | units of debentures has not been registered by the
-- src:39156 | Authority under section 240A; or
-- src:39158 | (b) a pricing statement in respect of the offer of debentures or
-- src:39159 | units of debentures has been registered by the Authority
-- src:39160 | under section 240A, and —
-- src:39162 | (i) the offer has closed with no application to subscribe
-- src:39163 | for or purchase the debentures or units of debentures
-- src:39164 | having been received or accepted; or
-- src:39166 | (ii) one or more applications to subscribe for or purchase
-- src:39167 | the debentures or units of debentures have been
-- src:39168 | received or accepted, and —
-- src:39170 | (A) in a case where the debentures or units of
-- src:39171 | debentures are or will be listed for quotation on
-- src:39172 | an approved exchange, trading in them has
-- src:39173 | commenced; or
-- src:39175 | (B) in any other case, all of those debentures or
-- src:39176 | units of debentures have been issued or sold.
@ref s 241(1C) (src:39151-39176)
GIVEN
    `a pricing statement in respect of the offer has been registered by the Authority under section 240A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority registered a pricing statement in respect of the offer of debentures or units of debentures under section 240A?
    `the offer has closed with no application to subscribe for or purchase having been received or accepted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the offer closed with no application to subscribe for or purchase the debentures or units of debentures having been received or accepted?
    `one or more applications to subscribe for or purchase have been received or accepted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have one or more applications to subscribe for or purchase the debentures or units of debentures been received or accepted?
    `the debentures or units of debentures are or will be listed for quotation on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the debentures or units of debentures, or will they be, listed for quotation on an approved exchange?
    `trading in them has commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has trading in them commenced?
    `all of those debentures or units of debentures have been issued or sold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all of those debentures or units of debentures been issued or sold?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(1C) the offer is not treated as subsisting` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a pricing statement in respect of the offer has been registered by the Authority under section 240A`) OR (`the offer has closed with no application to subscribe for or purchase having been received or accepted`) OR (`one or more applications to subscribe for or purchase have been received or accepted` AND ((`the debentures or units of debentures are or will be listed for quotation on an approved exchange` AND `trading in them has commenced`) OR ((NOT `the debentures or units of debentures are or will be listed for quotation on an approved exchange`) AND `all of those debentures or units of debentures have been issued or sold`)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an offer is not treated as subsisting if (a) a pricing statement in respect of the offer of debentures or units of debentures has not been registered by the Authority under section 240A; or (b) a pricing statement in respect of the offer of debentures or units of debentures has been registered by the Authority under section 240A, and (i) the offer has closed with no application to subscribe for or purchase the debentures or units of debentures having been received or accepted; or (ii) one or more applications to subscribe for or purchase the debentures or units of debentures have been received or accepted, and (A) in a case where the debentures or units of debentures are or will be listed for quotation on an approved exchange, trading in them has commenced; or (B) in any other case, all of those debentures or units of debentures have been issued or sold"  -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

§ `s 241(2) to (7): what the document must contain, and what the person making the offer must do`

-- s 241(2): the beginning of a supplementary document. A duty: scope is the supplementary document (NOTHING outside it).
-- src:39183 | (2) At the beginning of a supplementary document, there must
-- src:39184 | be —
-- src:39186 | (a) a statement that it is a supplementary prospectus or a
-- src:39187 | supplementary profile statement, as the case may be;
-- src:39189 | (b) an identification of the prospectus or profile statement it
-- src:39190 | supplements;
-- src:39192 | (c) an identification of any previous supplementary document
-- src:39193 | lodged with the Authority in relation to the offer; and
-- src:39195 | (d) a statement that it is to be read together with the prospectus
-- src:39196 | or profile statement it supplements and any previous
-- src:39197 | supplementary document in relation to the offer.
@ref s 241(2) (src:39183-39197)
GIVEN
    `the document is a supplementary document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a supplementary document?
    `it begins with a statement that it is a supplementary prospectus or a supplementary profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document begin with a statement that it is a supplementary prospectus or a supplementary profile statement, as the case may be?
    `it begins with an identification of the prospectus or profile statement it supplements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document begin with an identification of the prospectus or profile statement it supplements?
    `it begins with an identification of any previous supplementary document lodged with the Authority in relation to the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document begin with an identification of any previous supplementary document lodged with the Authority in relation to the offer (answer yes if there is none to identify)?
    `it begins with a statement that it is to be read together with the prospectus or profile statement it supplements and any previous supplementary document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document begin with a statement that it is to be read together with the prospectus or profile statement it supplements and any previous supplementary document in relation to the offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(2) the supplementary document begins as it must` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the document is a supplementary document`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "At the beginning of a supplementary document, there must be"
        IF `it begins with a statement that it is a supplementary prospectus or a supplementary profile statement` AND `it begins with an identification of the prospectus or profile statement it supplements` AND `it begins with an identification of any previous supplementary document lodged with the Authority in relation to the offer` AND `it begins with a statement that it is to be read together with the prospectus or profile statement it supplements and any previous supplementary document`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "At the beginning of a supplementary document, there must be (a) a statement that it is a supplementary prospectus or a supplementary profile statement, as the case may be; (b) an identification of the prospectus or profile statement it supplements; (c) an identification of any previous supplementary document lodged with the Authority in relation to the offer; and (d) a statement that it is to be read together with the prospectus or profile statement it supplements and any previous supplementary document in relation to the offer"

-- s 241(3): the beginning of a replacement document.
-- src:39199 | (3) At the beginning of a replacement document, there must be —
-- src:39201 | (a) a statement that it is a replacement prospectus or a
-- src:39202 | replacement profile statement, as the case may be; and
-- src:39204 | (b) an identification of the prospectus or profile statement it
-- src:39205 | replaces.
@ref s 241(3) (src:39199-39205)
GIVEN
    `the document is a replacement document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a replacement document?
    `it begins with a statement that it is a replacement prospectus or a replacement profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document begin with a statement that it is a replacement prospectus or a replacement profile statement, as the case may be?
    `it begins with an identification of the prospectus or profile statement it replaces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the document begin with an identification of the prospectus or profile statement it replaces?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(3) the replacement document begins as it must` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the document is a replacement document`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "At the beginning of a replacement document, there must be"
        IF `it begins with a statement that it is a replacement prospectus or a replacement profile statement` AND `it begins with an identification of the prospectus or profile statement it replaces`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "At the beginning of a replacement document, there must be (a) a statement that it is a replacement prospectus or a replacement profile statement, as the case may be; and (b) an identification of the prospectus or profile statement it replaces"

-- s 241(4): the document is dated with the date of lodgment.
-- src:39207 | (4) The supplementary document and the replacement document
-- src:39208 | must be dated with the date on which they are lodged with the
-- src:39209 | Authority.
@ref s 241(4) (src:39207-39209)
GIVEN
    `the document is a supplementary document or a replacement document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a supplementary document or a replacement document?
    `the date the document bears` IS A DATE @desc What date does the document bear?
    `the date the document is lodged with the Authority` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the document lodged with the Authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(4) the document is dated with the date on which it is lodged` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the document is a supplementary document or a replacement document`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The supplementary document and the replacement document must be dated"
        IF `the date the document bears` EQUALS `the date the document is lodged with the Authority`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be dated with the date on which they are lodged with the Authority"

-- s 241(5): the person making the offer must take reasonable steps.
-- src:39211 | (5) The person making the offer must take reasonable steps —
-- src:39213 | (a) to inform potential investors of the lodgment of any
-- src:39214 | supplementary or replacement document under
-- src:39215 | subsection (1) or (1A); and
-- src:39217 | (b) to make available to them the supplementary document or
-- src:39218 | replacement document.
@ref s 241(5) (src:39211-39218)
GIVEN
    `a supplementary or replacement document has been lodged under subsection (1) or (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a supplementary or replacement document been lodged under section 241(1) or (1A)?
    `the person making the offer has taken reasonable steps to inform potential investors of the lodgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you taken reasonable steps to inform potential investors of the lodgment?
    `the person making the offer has taken reasonable steps to make the document available to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you taken reasonable steps to make the supplementary document or replacement document available to them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(5) the person making the offer has taken the reasonable steps` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a supplementary or replacement document has been lodged under subsection (1) or (1A)`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to inform potential investors of the lodgment of any supplementary or replacement document under subsection (1) or (1A)"
        IF `the person making the offer has taken reasonable steps to inform potential investors of the lodgment` AND `the person making the offer has taken reasonable steps to make the document available to them`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The person making the offer must take reasonable steps (a) to inform potential investors of the lodgment of any supplementary or replacement document under subsection (1) or (1A); and (b) to make available to them the supplementary document or replacement document"

-- s 241(6) and (6B): what the prospectus or profile statement is taken to be after a supplementary or replacement document. Each is a "where" paragraph: JUST FALSE when it fails (rule (b)).
-- src:39220 | (6) For the purposes of the application of this Division to events
-- src:39221 | that occur after the lodgment of the supplementary document —
-- src:39223 | (a) where the supplementary document is a supplementary
-- src:39224 | prospectus, the prospectus in relation to the offer is taken to
-- src:39225 | be the original prospectus together with the supplementary
-- src:39226 | prospectus and any previous supplementary prospectus in
-- src:39227 | relation to the offer; and
@ref s 241(6)(a) (src:39220-39227)
GIVEN
    `the events occur after the lodgment of the supplementary document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question about events that occur after the lodgment of the supplementary document?
    `the supplementary document is a supplementary prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the supplementary document a supplementary prospectus?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(6)(a) the prospectus in relation to the offer is taken to be the original prospectus with the supplementary prospectus and any previous one` MEANS
    IF `the events occur after the lodgment of the supplementary document` AND `the supplementary document is a supplementary prospectus`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purposes of the application of this Division to events that occur after the lodgment of the supplementary document (a) where the supplementary document is a supplementary prospectus, the prospectus in relation to the offer is taken to be the original prospectus together with the supplementary prospectus and any previous supplementary prospectus in relation to the offer"

-- src:39232 | (b) where the supplementary document is a supplementary
-- src:39233 | profile statement, the profile statement in relation to the
-- src:39234 | offer is taken to be the original profile statement together
-- src:39235 | with the supplementary profile statement and any previous
-- src:39236 | supplementary profile statement in relation to the offer.
@ref s 241(6)(b) (src:39232-39236)
GIVEN
    `the events occur after the lodgment of the supplementary document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question about events that occur after the lodgment of the supplementary document?
    `the supplementary document is a supplementary profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the supplementary document a supplementary profile statement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(6)(b) the profile statement in relation to the offer is taken to be the original profile statement with the supplementary profile statement and any previous one` MEANS
    IF `the events occur after the lodgment of the supplementary document` AND `the supplementary document is a supplementary profile statement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the supplementary document is a supplementary profile statement, the profile statement in relation to the offer is taken to be the original profile statement together with the supplementary profile statement and any previous supplementary profile statement in relation to the offer"

-- src:39240 | (6B) For the purposes of the application of this Division to events
-- src:39241 | that occur after the lodgment of the replacement document —
-- src:39243 | (a) where the replacement document is a replacement
-- src:39244 | prospectus, the prospectus in relation to the offer is taken
-- src:39245 | to be the replacement prospectus; and
@ref s 241(6B)(a) (src:39240-39245)
GIVEN
    `the events occur after the lodgment of the replacement document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question about events that occur after the lodgment of the replacement document?
    `the replacement document is a replacement prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the replacement document a replacement prospectus?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(6B)(a) the prospectus in relation to the offer is taken to be the replacement prospectus` MEANS
    IF `the events occur after the lodgment of the replacement document` AND `the replacement document is a replacement prospectus`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purposes of the application of this Division to events that occur after the lodgment of the replacement document (a) where the replacement document is a replacement prospectus, the prospectus in relation to the offer is taken to be the replacement prospectus"

-- src:39247 | (b) where the replacement document is a replacement profile
-- src:39248 | statement, the profile statement in relation to the offer is
-- src:39249 | taken to be the replacement profile statement.
@ref s 241(6B)(b) (src:39247-39249)
GIVEN
    `the events occur after the lodgment of the replacement document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question about events that occur after the lodgment of the replacement document?
    `the replacement document is a replacement profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the replacement document a replacement profile statement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(6B)(b) the profile statement in relation to the offer is taken to be the replacement profile statement` MEANS
    IF `the events occur after the lodgment of the replacement document` AND `the replacement document is a replacement profile statement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the replacement document is a replacement profile statement, the profile statement in relation to the offer is taken to be the replacement profile statement"

-- s 241(7): the offer must be kept open for at least 14 days after the lodgment. A duty with an "If" gate: NOTHING when no document is lodged (fork F18).
-- src:39251 | (7) If a supplementary document or replacement document is
-- src:39252 | lodged with the Authority, the offer must be kept open for at least
-- src:39253 | 14 days after the lodgment of the supplementary document or
-- src:39254 | replacement document.
@ref s 241(7) (src:39251-39254)
GIVEN
    `a supplementary document or replacement document is lodged with the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a supplementary document or replacement document lodged with the Authority?
    `the date of lodgment of the supplementary document or replacement document` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the supplementary document or replacement document lodged with the Authority?
    `the date until which the offer is kept open` IS A DATE @desc Until what date is the offer kept open (the last day on which it can be accepted)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(7) the offer has been kept open for at least 14 days after the lodgment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a supplementary document or replacement document is lodged with the Authority`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a supplementary document or replacement document is lodged with the Authority, the offer must be kept open"
        IF `the date until which the offer is kept open` AT LEAST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of lodgment of the supplementary document or replacement document` 14 Days)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the offer must be kept open for at least 14 days after the lodgment of the supplementary document or replacement document"

§ `s 241(8) to (11): applicants who applied to subscribe, before the document was lodged`

-- s 241(8)(a): the "where" gate of the paragraph (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b): when a "where" fails the answer is JUST FALSE).
-- src:39256 | (8) Where, prior to the lodgment of the supplementary document or
-- src:39257 | replacement document, applications have been made under the
-- src:39258 | original prospectus or profile statement to subscribe for securities or
-- src:39259 | securities‑based derivatives contracts, then —
-- src:39261 | (a) where the securities or securities‑based derivatives
