`s 241(11) the applicant has notified the person making the offer and returned the documents within 14 days` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the applicant wishes to exercise the option under subsection (8)(b)(i) or (ii) to return the securities or contracts`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An applicant who wishes to exercise the applicant's option under subsection (8)(b)(i) or (ii) to return securities or securities-based derivatives contracts issued to the applicant must"
        IF `the applicant notified the person making the offer` AND (`the date of the notification` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of lodgment of the supplementary document or replacement document` 14 Days)) AND `the applicant returned all documents purporting to be evidence of title` AND (`the date the documents were returned` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of lodgment of the supplementary document or replacement document` 14 Days))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, within 14 days from the date of lodgment of the supplementary document or replacement document, notify the person making the offer of this and return all documents (if any) purporting to be evidence of title to those securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to that person"

@ref s 241(11) (the person's payment) (src:39382-39394)
GIVEN
    `the applicant notified the person making the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the applicant notify you that the applicant returns the securities or contracts?
    `the date the notification was received` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive the notification?
    `the date the documents were received` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive the documents purporting to be evidence of title (the date of the notification if there are none)?
    `the person making the offer paid the applicant all moneys paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pay the applicant all moneys the applicant paid for the securities or contracts?
    `the date the moneys were paid` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you pay the applicant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(11) the person making the offer has paid the applicant within 7 days from the receipt of the notification and documents` MEANS
    IF `the applicant notified the person making the offer` AND `the person making the offer paid the applicant all moneys paid` AND (`the date the moneys were paid` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` (IF `the date the documents were received` AT LEAST `the date the notification was received` THEN `the date the documents were received` ELSE `the date the notification was received`) 7 Days))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "upon which that person must, within 7 days from the receipt of such notification and documents (if any) pay to the applicant all moneys paid by the applicant for the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts"

@ref s 241(11) (the deeming) (src:39392-39394)
GIVEN
    `the applicant returned the securities or contracts under subsection (8)(b)(i) or (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the applicant exercise the option to return the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts issued to the applicant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(11) the issue of the securities or contracts is deemed to be void` MEANS
    IF `the applicant returned the securities or contracts under subsection (8)(b)(i) or (ii)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and the issue of those securities or securities-based derivatives contracts is deemed to be void" reaches the securities returned under the option and says nothing of any other issue

