        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an answer of a route was not worked out
-- s 241(13): the applicant who wishes to withdraw must notify within 14 days; the person making the offer must then pay within 7 days from the receipt.
-- src:39535 | (13) An applicant who wishes to exercise the applicant’s option
-- src:39536 | under subsection (12)(a)(i) or (ii) to withdraw the applicant’s
-- src:39537 | application must, within 14 days from the date of lodgment of the
-- src:39538 | supplementary document or replacement document, notify the person
-- src:39539 | making the offer of this, upon which that person must, within 7 days
-- src:39540 | of the receipt of such notification, pay to the applicant all moneys
-- src:39541 | paid by the applicant on account of the applicant’s application for the
-- src:39542 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts.
@ref s 241(13) (the applicant's notice) (src:39535-39542)
GIVEN
    `the applicant wishes to exercise the option under subsection (12)(a)(i) or (ii) to withdraw the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you wish to exercise your option under section 241(12)(a)(i) or (ii) to withdraw your application?
    `the date of lodgment of the supplementary document or replacement document` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the supplementary document or replacement document lodged with the Authority?
    `the applicant notified the person making the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you notify the person making the offer that you wish to withdraw your application?
    `the date of the notification` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you notify the person making the offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(13) the applicant has notified the person making the offer within 14 days` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the applicant wishes to exercise the option under subsection (12)(a)(i) or (ii) to withdraw the application`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An applicant who wishes to exercise the applicant's option under subsection (12)(a)(i) or (ii) to withdraw the applicant's application must"
        IF `the applicant notified the person making the offer` AND (`the date of the notification` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of lodgment of the supplementary document or replacement document` 14 Days))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, within 14 days from the date of lodgment of the supplementary document or replacement document, notify the person making the offer of this"

@ref s 241(13) (the person's payment) (src:39535-39542)
GIVEN
    `the applicant notified the person making the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the applicant notify you that the applicant wishes to withdraw the application?
    `the date the notification was received` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive the notification?
    `the person making the offer paid the applicant all moneys paid on account of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pay the applicant all moneys the applicant paid on account of the application?
    `the date the moneys were paid` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you pay the applicant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(13) the person making the offer has paid the applicant within 7 days of the receipt of the notification` MEANS
    IF `the applicant notified the person making the offer` AND `the person making the offer paid the applicant all moneys paid on account of the application` AND (`the date the moneys were paid` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the notification was received` 7 Days))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "upon which that person must, within 7 days of the receipt of such notification, pay to the applicant all moneys paid by the applicant on account of the applicant's application"

-- s 241(14): the applicant who wishes to return must notify within 14 days and return the title documents; the person must then pay within 7 days; the sale is deemed void.
-- src:39546 | (14) An applicant who wishes to exercise the applicant’s option
-- src:39547 | under subsection (12)(b)(i) or (ii) to return securities or
-- src:39548 | securities‑based derivatives contracts sold to the applicant must,
-- src:39549 | within 14 days from the date of lodgment of the supplementary
-- src:39550 | document or replacement document, notify the person making the
-- src:39551 | offer of this and return all documents (if any) purporting to evidence
-- src:39552 | title to those securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts to the
-- src:39553 | person making the offer, upon which that person must, within 7 days
-- src:39558 | from the receipt of such notification and documents (if any) pay to the
-- src:39559 | applicant all moneys paid by the applicant for the securities or
-- src:39560 | securities‑based derivatives contracts and the sale of the securities or
-- src:39561 | securities‑based derivatives contracts is deemed to be void.
@ref s 241(14) (the applicant's notice and documents) (src:39546-39561)
GIVEN
    `the applicant wishes to exercise the option under subsection (12)(b)(i) or (ii) to return the securities or contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you wish to exercise your option under section 241(12)(b)(i) or (ii) to return the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts sold to you?
    `the date of lodgment of the supplementary document or replacement document` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the supplementary document or replacement document lodged with the Authority?
    `the applicant notified the person making the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you notify the person making the offer that you wish to return the securities or contracts?
    `the date of the notification` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you notify the person making the offer?
    `the applicant returned all documents purporting to evidence title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you return all documents (if any) purporting to evidence title to the securities or contracts to the person making the offer (answer yes if there are none)?
    `the date the documents were returned` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you return the documents (any date if there are none)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(14) the applicant has notified the person making the offer and returned the documents within 14 days` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the applicant wishes to exercise the option under subsection (12)(b)(i) or (ii) to return the securities or contracts`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An applicant who wishes to exercise the applicant's option under subsection (12)(b)(i) or (ii) to return securities or securities-based derivatives contracts sold to the applicant must"
        IF `the applicant notified the person making the offer` AND (`the date of the notification` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of lodgment of the supplementary document or replacement document` 14 Days)) AND `the applicant returned all documents purporting to evidence title` AND (`the date the documents were returned` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of lodgment of the supplementary document or replacement document` 14 Days))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, within 14 days from the date of lodgment of the supplementary document or replacement document, notify the person making the offer of this and return all documents (if any) purporting to evidence title to those securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to the person making the offer"

@ref s 241(14) (the person's payment) (src:39546-39561)
GIVEN
    `the applicant notified the person making the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the applicant notify you that the applicant returns the securities or contracts?
    `the date the notification was received` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive the notification?
    `the date the documents were received` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive the documents purporting to evidence title (the date of the notification if there are none)?
    `the person making the offer paid the applicant all moneys paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pay the applicant all moneys the applicant paid for the securities or contracts?
    `the date the moneys were paid` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you pay the applicant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(14) the person making the offer has paid the applicant within 7 days from the receipt of the notification and documents` MEANS
    IF `the applicant notified the person making the offer` AND `the person making the offer paid the applicant all moneys paid` AND (`the date the moneys were paid` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` (IF `the date the documents were received` AT LEAST `the date the notification was received` THEN `the date the documents were received` ELSE `the date the notification was received`) 7 Days))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "upon which that person must, within 7 days from the receipt of such notification and documents (if any) pay to the applicant all moneys paid by the applicant for the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts"

@ref s 241(14) (the deeming) (src:39560-39561)
GIVEN
    `the applicant returned the securities or contracts under subsection (12)(b)(i) or (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the applicant exercise the option to return the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts sold to the applicant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(14) the sale of the securities or contracts is deemed to be void` MEANS
    IF `the applicant returned the securities or contracts under subsection (12)(b)(i) or (ii)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and the sale of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts is deemed to be void" reaches the securities returned under the option and says nothing of any other sale

§ `s 241(15) to (17): offences, and what a statement includes`

-- s 241(15): the offence of contravening subsection (8) or (12), and its penalty. Contravening (8)(a) is being bound by it and not meeting it.
-- src:39565 | (15) Any person who contravenes subsection (8) or (12) shall be
-- src:39566 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:39567 | exceeding $100,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a
-- src:39568 | further fine not exceeding $10,000 for every day or part of a day
-- src:39569 | during which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 241(15) (src:39565-39569)
GIVEN
    `whether the person is bound by section 241(8)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 241(8)(a) the person making the offer is bound by paragraph (a)` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `whether the person has met section 241(8)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 241(8)(a) the person making the offer has met one of the routes` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `whether the person is bound by section 241(8)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 241(8)(b) the person making the offer is bound by paragraph (b)` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `whether the person has met section 241(8)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 241(8)(b) the person making the offer has met one of the routes` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `whether the person is bound by section 241(12)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 241(12)(a) the person making the offer is bound by paragraph (a)` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `whether the person has met section 241(12)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 241(12)(a) the person making the offer has met one of the routes` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `whether the person is bound by section 241(12)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 241(12)(b) the person making the offer is bound by paragraph (b)` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `whether the person has met section 241(12)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 241(12)(b) the person making the offer has met one of the routes` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F19 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 241(15) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF ((`whether the person is bound by section 241(8)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`whether the person has met section 241(8)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) OR ((`whether the person is bound by section 241(8)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`whether the person has met section 241(8)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) OR ((`whether the person is bound by section 241(12)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`whether the person has met section 241(12)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) OR ((`whether the person is bound by section 241(12)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`whether the person has met section 241(12)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF ((`whether the person is bound by section 241(8)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`whether the person has met section 241(8)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) AND ((`whether the person is bound by section 241(8)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`whether the person has met section 241(8)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) AND ((`whether the person is bound by section 241(12)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`whether the person has met section 241(12)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) AND ((`whether the person is bound by section 241(12)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`whether the person has met section 241(12)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who contravenes subsection (8) or (12) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an answer under subsection (8) or (12) was not worked out

@ref s 241(15) (the penalty) (src:39565-39569)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 241(15) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 100000, 0, FALSE, 10000  -- a fine not exceeding $100,000; no imprisonment is stated (0); a further fine not exceeding $10,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

-- s 241(16): the offence of contravening any other provision of the section, and its penalty. The answers of the duty functions are passed in as a list; JUST FALSE in the list means the duty was not met.
-- src:39571 | (16) Any person who contravenes any other provision of this
-- src:39572 | section shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:39573 | to a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:39574 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of
-- src:39575 | a day during which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 241(16) (src:39571-39575)
GIVEN
    `the answers of the other duties in this section` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What do the functions for the duties of section 241(2), (3), (4), (5), (7), (10), (11), (13) and (14) answer for the person? (List each answer: JUST TRUE if the duty was met, JUST FALSE if it was not, NOTHING if it does not arise.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F20 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 241(16) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF elem (JUST FALSE) `the answers of the other duties in this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who contravenes any other provision of this section shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)

@ref s 241(16) (the penalty) (src:39571-39575)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 241(16) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000  -- a fine not exceeding $50,000; no imprisonment is stated (0); a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

-- s 241(17): the reference to a statement in subsection (1)(a) includes information presented in any form.
-- src:39577 | (17) For the purposes of subsection (1)(a), the reference to a
-- src:39578 | statement includes a reference to any information presented,
-- src:39579 | regardless of whether such information is in text or otherwise.
@ref s 241(17) (src:39577-39579)
GIVEN
    `the information is presented, whether in text or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information presented in the prospectus or profile statement, whether in text or otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(17) the information presented is a statement for the purposes of subsection (1)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the information is presented, whether in text or otherwise`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the reference to a statement includes a reference to any information presented" lists without closing the list

